docs/implementation-spec.md:1931:**R-9.12** Old payloads are never re-signed. A superseding attestation wraps the original package and signs that with the new-algorithm key; the inner attestation's bytes, signatures and OTS proof are immutable, and the wrapper is a new layer with its own time-anchor. Nesting depth is bounded by willingness to pay, not by a protocol cap. [REGISTERED prereg §3.1, docs/phase-0-prereg.md:339-355]
docs/implementation-spec.md:1933:**R-9.13** One permanently reserved unrecognized algorithm identifier remains in the test suite after a real PQ provider lands, so the `UNVERIFIABLE` path is exercised forever, and a conformance vector ships in the bundle's fixed floor: "a signature in an algorithm you do not know; the correct verdict is `UNVERIFIABLE`." [REGISTERED A3 §A3.6.2, docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-3.md:513-520]
