    15	## 1. The accepted domain, exactly
    16	
    17	Let **V** be the set of JSON values in E§1.1:
    18	- `null`, `true` and `false`;
    19	- finite binary64 numbers other than −0;
    20	- strings of Unicode scalar values that contain no noncharacter, no code point unassigned in Unicode 16.0.0, and are
    21	  in NFC;
    22	- arrays;
    23	- objects with pairwise distinct names.
    24	
    25	Two values are **equal** when they are equal as mathematical structures:
    26	- numbers are equal as doubles;
    27	- strings are equal as scalar sequences;
    28	- arrays are equal as sequences;
    29	- objects are equal as finite maps from names to values. Member order is not part of an object.
    30	
    31	That is the sense in which injectivity is claimed. Two JSON *texts* that differ only in spelling denote one value,
    32	and E§1.2 says why that is intended.
    33	
    34	The accepted sets are:
    35	
    36	- **Payloads.** For a tag `t`, `Pay(t) = { JCS(v) : v ∈ V, Schema_t(v), depth(v) ≤ 64, |JCS(v)| ≤ 2^24 }`. Here
    37	  `Schema_attest` is E§3.2 together with E§3.3, and `Schema_manifest` is E§4.
    38	- **Frames.** `Frm(t) = { frame(t, p) : p ∈ Pay(t) }` for `t ∈ {attest, manifest}`, where
    39	  `frame(t, p) = [|t|] ‖ t ‖ 00 01 ‖ u32(|p|) ‖ p`.
    40	- **Anchor preimages.** `Anc = { A(F0, F1) : F0, F1 ∈ Frm(attest) }`, where
    41	  `A(F0, F1) = [25] ‖ "tessera-v1/receipt-anchor" ‖ 02 ‖ u32|F0| ‖ F0 ‖ u32|F1| ‖ F1`.
    42	- **Snapshot preimages.** `Snp = { S(s) : 1 ≤ |s| ≤ 2^24 }`, where `S(s) = [26] ‖ "tessera-v1/dnssec-snapshot" ‖ u32|s| ‖ s`.
    43	- **Receipts.** A tuple `(F_M, F_0, F_1, A)` is an *accepted receipt* when all of the following hold:
    44	  - `F_M ∈ Frm(manifest)` decodes to a manifest `M`;
    45	  - `F_0` and `F_1` are in `Frm(attest)` and decode to `(C_0, fp_0)` and `(C_1, fp_1)`;
    46	  - `fp_0 = M.key_fp` and `fp_1 = M.sset[0]`;
    47	  - `JCS(C_0) = JCS(C_1)`;
    48	  - `C_0.manifest_sha256 = hex(SHA256(F_M))`, and `C_0.issuer` and `C_0.alg` equal those of `M`;
